  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "findings_f3855a3dc002867772ae",
      "text": "Two different loading processes have fed this table over the years. The old one stopped running in 2020 (15,019,410 rows, frozen). The current one runs daily and touched data again this morning (6,958,825 rows)",
    },
    {
      "id": "findings_2d6ef3d7032115507cd0",
      "text": "Serious: the step meant to keep household level benefit flags correct only looks at households that still exist in the staging table frozen since 2020. Any household created or changed since then is silently skipped, its benefit flags never get re-evaluated",
    },
    {
      "id": "findings_ca9c2832ca50f2775228",
      "text": "Serious, same root cause: the step meant to correct a card's points earning flag also only compares against that same frozen 2020 staging table. For any card active since then, there is no working mechanism left in this table's process to ever fix that flag once it goes wrong",
    },
    {
      "id": "findings_5990ce180b6278f8dad0",
      "text": "Confirmed: the final step into this table inserts new cards and updates existing ones by matching the internal key. Every update also overwrites the basket discount and points earning flags with whatever the staging table has, which, as found above, is empty from the true source. This is not a hypothesis anymore, it is confirmed in code: any card touched by today's process loses these two settings",
    },
    {
      "id": "findings_bf03407a749634a7ea39",
      "text": "Confirmed: the step that copies data from the raw feed into the next staging table always marks every card as approved, and computes a fingerprint used to detect what changed. That fingerprint is built from name, address and contact fields only. A card whose only change is to its discount or points settings would not be picked up as changed at all",
    },
    {
      "id": "findings_38bce940215784c76b32",
      "text": "26 other tables depend on this one, including the two largest transaction tables in the warehouse. This table has to be migrated before any of them",
    },
  ],
